{
  "dom_id": "step-q145109",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\,0<x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{2}\\,x \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{4}<Y\\,|\\,X=\\frac{3}{2}).$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(Y\\in A\\,|\\,X=x)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{4}<Y\\,|\\,X=\\frac{3}{2}) & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{3\\sqrt{2}/2}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x=\\frac{3}{2})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{3\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{y}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{\\int }_{1/4}^{3\\sqrt{2}/2}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{1/4}^{3\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}({(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot \\frac{71}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{71}{72}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
